----------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe Galois Alperin weight conjecture for finite category algebras (https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.06166)\nciteturn5academia12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 months ago; Authors: Xin HuangDate: Tue Apr  7 17:58:57 2026 ... If $\\mathcal{C}$ is an EI-category, we can give a partition of weights of $k\\mathcal{O}_{\\mathcal{C}}$ with respect to blocks of $k\\mathcal{C}$ and formulate a blockwise Galois Alperin weight conjecture (BGAWC) for $\\mathcal{C}$.\nTitle: The Galois Alperin weight conjecture for finite category algebras\nAuthors: Xin Huang\nDate: Tue Apr  7 17:58:57 2026\n\nLet $p$ be a prime, $k$ an algebraic closure of $\\mathbb{F}_p$ and $Γ$ the Galois group ${\\rm Gal}(k/\\mathbb{F}_p)$. Let $\\mathcal{C}$ be a finite category and $\\mathcal{O}_{\\mathcal{C}}$ the $p$-orbit category of $\\mathcal{C}$ defined by Linckelmann. We formulate a version of the Galois Alperin weight conjecture (GAWC) for finite category algebras stating that there exists a $Γ$-equivariant bijection between the set of isomorphism classes of simple $k\\mathcal{C}$-modules and that of the weight algebra $W(k\\mathcal{O}_{\\mathcal{C}})$. We show that the versions of the GAWC for finite groups and for finite categories are in fact equivalent. If $\\mathcal{C}$ is an EI-category, we can give a partition of weights of $k\\mathcal{O}_{\\mathcal{C}}$ with respect to blocks of $k\\mathcal{C}$ and formulate a blockwise Galois Alperin weight conjecture (BGAWC) for $\\mathcal{C}$. We show that the versions of the BGAWC for finite groups and for finite EI-categories are equivalent.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe blockwise Galois Alperin Weight Conjecture for symmetric and alternating groups | Mathematische Zeitschrift | Springer Nature Link (https://doi.org/10.1007/s00209-025-03803-w?urlappend=%3Futm_source%3Dresearchgate.net%26utm_medium%3Darticle)\nciteturn5search2 [wor