 of quotient groups of its local subgroups. This conjecture has been reduced to inductive conditions of finite simple groups, that is, to prove this conjecture, it suffices to prove the inductive Alperin weight conditions for finite simple groups. In this lecture, we prove the blockwise Galois Alperin weight conjecture for 2-covering groups of symmetric and alternating groups. This is a joint work with Xin Huang and Jiping Zhang.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAlperin’s weight conjecture, Galois automorphisms, alternating (https://yilmazdeniz.bilkent.edu.tr/papers/awc-galois-functorial.pdf)\nciteturn5search15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8 months ago; We show that functorial equivalences can oﬀer new insight into the blockwise Galois Alperin ... For example, in [3, Theorem 10.6], Bouc and Yılmaz investigated the Dono- ... show that functorial equivalences may also shed light on the blockwise Galois Alperin weight ... Email addresses: xinhuang@mails.ccnu.edu.cn (Xin Huang), d.yilmaz@bilkent.edu.tr (Deniz\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nVirtual Morita equivalences and Brauer character bijections (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/380984902_Virtual_Morita_equivalences_and_Brauer_character_bijections)\nciteturn5search11 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago;   * Xin Huang ... The blockwise Galois Alperin Weight Conjecture for symmetric and alternating groups ... We prove that the blockwise Galois Alperin Weight Conjecture holds for symmetric and alternating groups.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nA reduction theorem for the blockwise Galois (https://www.znakschoola.ru/?_=%2Fpdf%2F2512.15243%23UE7DkG0PaBHZOakR54g1Wl8%3D)\nciteturn5search16 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7 months ago; blockwise Galois Alperin weight (BGAW) conjecture (see Conjecture 1.1) and establish its re- ... Conjecture 1.1 (blockwise Galois Alp